s and  precision medicine based therapies are  being designed to cure  and treat cll it's responsible for the  induction of antigen and autonomous  signaling within the cells  also as i talked about the occurrence of  uncontrolled clonal division of b cells  it can occur due to various primary  factors such as antigenic stimulation  genetic mutations and previously  existing cytogenic genetic abnormalities  but the mbl can progress to chronic  lymphocytic leukemia  by the further insult to the b cell  clones due to genetic abnormalities or  in occurrence of infections or changes  within the bone marrow micro environment  this tumor micro environment is  receiving lots of attention when it  comes to its role of within cell  signaling and the  occurrence of normal  immune responses  that's why the tumor micro environment  is also being looked at as one of the  causes and its defects can also be used  to develop therapies against cll  the tumor micro environment represents a  highly complex cellular component  including non-hemopoietic stem cells  extracellular matrix lymphocytes and  myeloid cell subpopulations these  elements call for therapy resistance by  creating an immunosuppressive  environment  that's why the question or the goal  around which the project is designed is  to understand the molecular mechanisms  behind the interdependencies of  intra-tumor heterogeneity and tumor  micro environment in cll  so for this project the data set labeled  gse161711 was obtained from the jio  website 152 samples were obtained from  37 patients and this number of samples  exceeds the number of patients because  each patient gives three types of  samples it can be broadly categorized  into two categories namely peripheral  blood and the other one was from the  lymph node  the peripheral blood sample only  contained cd19 positive cells that were  filtered and extracted and the lymph  node gave two kinds of samples namely  cd19 positive cells that were filtered  and isolated 