ters and filtered out  those most significantly expressed genes  about 38 387 genes were massively  differentially expressed 353 upregulated  genes and 34 down regulated genes  were found and here's a snapshot of the  david tool how it looks like and how we  are able to correlate their ensemble ids  to their gene ids and the names of the  genes  so the differential gene expression when  we were able to look at their p values  and their existed values in the log two  fold chains which all helps us  understand  uh how how quantitatively how much of  the gene was expressed uh how high or  low the gene expression was and how  significantly it was expressed with the  help of the volcanoes 2r  we drew a volcano plot  and as we can see that  that the down regulated genes are  expressed by  blue dot and the upregulated genes are  expressed with the help of red dots we  put them on a graph where the y axis  shows the  negative locked in value of the  of the p existed or the p value and the  x axis talks about the log fold change  for the cd19 subgroup we see that  certain genes were the most  significantly uh  expressed and most upregulated such as  the  ami a1a gene which is the alpha amylase  pseudogene involved in the cellular  oligosaccharide metabolic processes  and  the am em53 gene which is the  transmembrane  protein 53 which is  responsible for transmembrane  translocation of various biomolecules  and  the mrpl20 gene which is the  mitochondrial  ribosomal gene which regulates the trans  location of mitochondria the pik3cd gene  which is the phosphatidyl inositol 4-5  bisphosphonate three kinase and it is  the catalytic subunit of this uh enzyme  which is involved in b cell  proliferation development and migration  of the b cell receptor signaling and it  also helps the t cell receptors perform  their signaling functions better and  also is  responsible for a very interesting  function which is the antigen dependent  memory of b cells  also some small nuclear associated rnas  such as  lsm10 and non-coding  rnas were also found that are involved  in tumor genesis with the regulation of  gene expression and their role in  differentiation of cells by regulation  of their receptors  the most downregulated genes involved  tnrp1 and acort7 which is the acyle  coenzyme a theostery7 it is a protein  coding gene and encodes  a member of the acyl coenzyme family  which is very essential in the fatty  acid metabolism  when we talk about the pathway analysis  plot of the cd90 gene we see that the  pathways most significantly um over  expressed or most significantly  associated with the occurrence of cll  for the samples of this cd19 plus true  subgroup are the not signaling pathway  and which is associate associated with  the interactions of tumor cells with the  micro environment angiogenesis pathway  the alzheimer's disease penicillin  pathway and the hf receptor signaling  pathway and the p53 pathway  when we talk about the molecular  functions plot we see that several  molecular functions are associated with  the differences occurring within the  lymph node and peripheral blood subgroup  which is the atp dependent  activity such as the chromo domain  helicase dna binding protein 5 that  binds to the dna by a histone protein  and it regulates gene transcription  hydrolysis molec micro tubule bound  binding and catalytic activity such as  phospholipid binding signal receptor  binding by phospholipase a2 family and  other members of the cyclin-dependent  protein serine theory theonene activity  now moving on to the lymph node subgroup  we see that in the lymph node subgroup a  similar volcano plot was drawn where the  upregulated cells were  denoted with the red  circles and the blues circles were  responsible for the  denoting of the  down degraded genes we see that several  top up regulated genes such as mthfr  which is the  methyl tetrahydrofolate reductase was  over expressed to a log phone change  changes 6.68 times and is involved 