d19 plus and  mixed  lymph node cells were variable  indicating differences in somatic  mutations and the interplay of immune  regulation  these observations of statistical  analysis identifies 1100 genes within  the lymph nodes and about 3700 genes in  the cd19 subgroup that was significantly  downregulated or upregulated it's  because of the recent advancements in  ngs and genome bytes sequencing that  have led to the understanding of  constantly mutated genes that play a  role in dna damage repair for example  tp53 chromatin modifications such as  hist1 h1e and pathway such as the notch  one signaling pathway the wnt pathway  and various other  inflammatory responses occurring in the  p cell  the functional role of myriads of  putative driving mutations have been  confirmed as gene silencing that results  in decreased cell viability and an  uncontrolled cloning expansion of  immature b cells  to conclude with the goal of this  project was to understand the up  regulated and down regulated gene  molecules associated pathways gene  products and cellular functions so that  new therapeutic targets and clinical  markets markers to predict the diagnosis  of cll patients could be understood  we noted that cll is an indolent  malignancy characterized by an increased  accumulation of cd19 positive and cd5  positive expressing cells  the tumor micro environment certainly  plays a very important role in the  prognosis of cll gene signatures  indicating the crosstalk between genetic  characteristics of cll along with those  of the immune micro environment  have been characterized by this  transcriptomic analysis  the players role in several cellular  pathways and these mutations can lead to  by a wide range of cellular consequences  such as aberrant dna repair altered pcr  signaling and an enhanced inflammatory  state in general  the critical molecular pathways such as  notch one which was the most expressed  pathway in both the subgroups and drives  chemokine signaling in t